==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l/en|middle earth}}
* {{l/en|Middle Earth}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|myddyl erthe|lang=enm}}, alteration (as if {{term|middel||middle|lang=enm}} + {{term|erthe||earth|lang=enm}}) of earlier {{term|middelerd|lang=enm}}, {{term|middenerd||middle-earth|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|middangeard|middanġeard|the globe, world, earth, mankind|lit=middle yard, middle inclosure, middle region|lang=ang}} (compare {{term|mid|lang=en}}, {{term|yard|lang=en}}), though often interpreted since Old English times as “middle + earth”. Cognate with {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|miðgarðr||Midgard|lang=is}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|𐌼𐌹𐌳𐌾𐌿𐌽𐌲𐌰𐍂𐌳𐍃||tr=midjungards|mid-yard, middle abode|lang=got}}. See {{term|Midgard|lang=en}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[middle]]-[[earth]]|-}}

# {{context|archaic|lang=en}} The physical world, as imagined between [[heaven]] and [[hell]], or pre-Christian equivalents.

